            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id4a0991dd">
               <p xml:id="idm165">Gade's first larger composition for a four part choir is dedicated to Constanze Schleinitz. She was married to the lawyer Heinrich Conrad Schleinitz, who was a member of the board of directors of the Gewandhaus Orchestra. They were close friends of Gade's during his stay in Leipzig. In 1862  Gade dedicated his five songs for male choir Op. 38 to Conrad Schleinitz.</p>
            </history>
